{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793358160,"nonce":"xew76XLc9mc354y6l66hkmq1H8c=","title":"Glass background brushes bypass material grouping, nesting and change detection","message":"The fluent background(GlassStyle) form already exists, but glass ownership detection in layout and app checks only Material::Glass. Native group planning rejects a Glass background, children do not receive the same glass depth/foreground ownership, and collected-content/backdrop discovery can miss the panel. Material painting ultimately emits Brush::Glass, so this difference is not a required rendering contract.\n\nThe owner requested closing these gaps and inconsistencies. Share effective glass detection/style resolution across supported paint and content-collection paths, preserve brush-specific parameters and explicit element overrides, support backdrop animation without replacing authored brush styling, and include glass configuration fields in change detection. Validate mixed material/brush nesting and supported grouping, live updates/replay, fallback and style preservation. Keep existing unsupported portal/Flow/3D guards. No public GroupGlass constructor or new nesting switch is needed.\n\nBaseline 3fad1735b41204c7f080f75b34784f2db1571c1b, plus pending documentation and focused tests. New test glass_brush_capture_derives_nesting_for_both_fluent_forms asserts first-level/nested command flags for both forms. Scope checks to touched paths and glass regressions. Release version/MSRV decisions remain in 3f77b11 and 373e03a; no publication/push.","files":null}]}